Oscar starts with 24 lollipops. He eats 2 on his way to school, so he has 24 - 2 = 22 lollipops left. He passes 14 out to his friends, so he has 22 - 14 = 8 lollipops left. He buys twice as many lollipops on his way home as he gave to his friends, so he buys 2 * 14 = 28 lollipops. He eats 3 more that night and 2 more in the morning, so he has 8 + 28 - 3 - 2 = 21 lollipops left.

Final answer: \boxed{21}
